ss=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1411561#post1411561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to be sure on something. This one is not covered in any of the kickstarter rewards presently, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it\u2019s a new book that is not part or goal of any KS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T14:39:30-07:00","id":1411567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1411561#post1411561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to be sure on something. This one is not covered in any of the kickstarter rewards presently, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. We didn't even know about Titanomachy when the Kickstarter was going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T14:49:05-07:00","id":1411570,"title":"","content":"I figured, but wanted to be sure I wasn't going to buy a book I already had coming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T14:57:27-07:00","id":1411572,"title":"","content":"Okay, reached the end, and yeah. Some of these Titans don't really belong there, but I think we can chalk that up to being the point a lot of the time. The Orishas' in-character lecture on how arbitrary the line can be is proof of that. Hell, some of them don't even seem interested in the Titanomachy; Rangda, Cernunnos, and Namazu come to mind (Rangda wishes to be left alone and support feminism, Namazu would be perfectly fine leaving Japan alone if someone figured out how to free her without collapsing the entire island chain, and Cernunnos is called out as not really being a Titan so much as he has a PTSD-induced Titanic Calling).<br /> <br /> Really, thinking on it, I think the Titanic Virtues being replaced with Titanic Callings might not be a bad thing. It emphasizes that Titans are still gods, albeit ambivalent ones, of their respective pantheons, and allows grudging alliances. Hell, the only truly bad guy I see is Tyrant; the others, even Monster, are dark, but could have socially productive ends (the Adversary breaking to heal could be a psychiatrist, the Primeval's desire for the world to remain untamed being an environmental consultant, the Destroyer is as much revolutionary as anarchist, and the Monster particularly amoral takes on Batman). It's not <i>easy, </i>especially with Monster, but it's hardly always evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T14:57:49-07:00","id":1411573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1411556#post1411556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That is emphatically not the premise this game is sold on.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean, its called The World because it isn't our world and clearly they have taken plenty of artistic license with the mythologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T15:17:06-07:00","id":1411574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1411573#post1411573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I mean, its called The World because it isn't our world and clearly they have taken plenty of artistic license with the mythologies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The difference being the elements of (various degrees of) ancient (to modern) myth are happening in public view with the consequential fallout. The myths not being the myths as advertised would defeat that premise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T16:03:02-07:00","id":1411582,"title":"","content":"Can I get the eratta reporting link please?<br /> The list of Fujin's Callings on page 27 is really bothering me; Fortune is a purview, and should not one of his Callings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T16:07:07-07:00","id":1411584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1411582#post1411582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I get the eratta reporting link please?<br /> The list of Fujin's Callings on page 27 is really bothering me; Fortune is a purview, and should not one of his Callings.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSevCA7KQY8tir2zT_ghLbV3x1Buh33BQwv26_QQqRpfSdQGnA/viewform\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSevCA7KQY8tir2zT_ghLbV3x1Buh33BQwv26_QQqRpfSdQGnA/viewform\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSevCA7KQY8tir2zT_ghLbV3x1Buh33BQwv26_QQqRpfSdQGnA/viewform\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSevCA7KQY8tir2zT_ghLbV3x1Buh33BQwv26_QQqRpfSdQGnA/viewform </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T16:07:12-07:00","id":1411585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1411572#post1411572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, some of them don't even seem interested in the Titanomachy; Rangda, Cernunnos, and Namazu come to mind (Rangda wishes to be left alone and support feminism, Namazu would be perfectly fine leaving Japan alone if someone figured out how to free her without collapsing the entire island chain, and Cernunnos is called out as not really being a Titan so much as he has a PTSD-induced Titanic Calling).</div> </div> </div> </div>Cernunnos does not give one hoot about the Titanomachy, and it makes me laugh that apparently people have called him 'evil.' He's not -- and indeed most of the Titans aren't 'evil,' and that sort of binary 'yes/no' thinking baffles me personally. What good would it be if we kept saying 'gosh, Titan is just a label that gets slapped on people, a lot of the time it doesn't mean that much' (which is said throughout the book repeatedly) if we didn't have an example of this one dude who got offered the ability to be an immortal dude being and said 'heck yeah, that's way better than trying to pass in Victorian England, sign me up, wait, what, Titanomachy? Mom, I don't care about this, bye, I'm gonna go party with Dionysus with my new ... staff.' <br /> <br /> He technically counts as a Titan because Domnu thought 'hey I can take this spare Mantle I found and make someone else on my side', and he exists largely to be an example of how Titans aren't evil; Titans can in fact not care about the Titanomachy very much; Titans (and Gods!) can be very different from their historical writeups because this is a game, and set in The World, not Our World; that the world is a living world in which Events Happen and change things from myth; and it's okay to make your Gods, Titans, etc. very very gay and trans if you want to, because why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25521-spider","name":"Spider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25521_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T16:10:28-07:00","id":1411587,"title":"","content":"In defense of Titanomachy I have to say that it is not a thing in any of the myths except for Theoi, and even them have some references of Cronos being released from Tartarus and Echidna being turned into a weird mammal that lay eggs and runs super fast as hedgehogs... wait, wrong echidna...<br /> <br /> The entire book is a game license on the myths to make a easier way to put scions of many pantheons working together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T16:17:43-07:00","id":1411588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1411585#post1411585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cernunnos does not give one hoot about the Titanomachy, and it makes me laugh that apparently people have called him 'evil.' He's not -- and indeed most of the Titans aren't 'evil,' and that sort of binary 'yes/no' thinking baffles me personally. What good would it be if we kept saying 'gosh, Titan is just a label that gets slapped on people, a lot of the time it doesn't mean that much' (which is said throughout the book repeatedly) if we didn't have an example of this one dude who got offered the ability to be an immortal dude being and said 'heck yeah, that's way better than trying to pass in Victorian England, sign me up, wait, what, Titanomachy? Mom, I don't care about this, bye, I'm gonna go party with Dionysus with my new ... staff.'<br /> <br /> He technically counts as a Titan because Domnu thought 'hey I can take this spare Mantle I found and make someone else on my side', and he exists largely to be an example of how Titans aren't evil; Titans can in fact not care about the Titanomachy very much; Titans (and Gods!) can be very different from their historical writeups because this is a game, and set in The World, not Our World; that the world is a living world in which Events Happen and change things from myth; and it's okay to make your Gods, Titans, etc. very very gay and trans if you want to, because why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely what I was picking up on. I especially like how many of antagonist characters are very easily people - I find it hilarious that Scorpion Men are actually kindly old grandparent sorts who also happen to be terrifying guardians.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, this book is good, because this is Surtr's theme song:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZYAPgPH9hsI\" data-code=\"ZYAPgPH9hsI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ZYAPgPH9hsI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T16:22:27-07:00","id":1411589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1411588#post1411588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Precisely what I was picking up on. I especially like how many of antagonist characters are very easily people - I find it hilarious that Scorpion Men are actually kindly old grandparent sorts who also happen to be terrifying guardians.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, this book is good, because this is Surtr's theme song:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZYAPgPH9hsI\" data-code=\"ZYAPgPH9hsI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ZYAPgPH9hsI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ... as the person who wrote Surtr, that is absolutely, absolutely the feel I was going for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> (And yes, Sif/Frigg is a typo, and exactly what the errata link is for.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25521-spider","name":"Spider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25521_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T16:26:07-07:00","id":1411590,"title":"","content":"I really like Primeval, and the collateral pool. I also like some of the birthright ideas like the DRAGON System","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T16:40:45-07:00","id":1411591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1411574#post1411574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The difference being the elements of (various degrees of) ancient (to modern) myth are happening in public view with the consequential fallout. The myths not being the myths as advertised would defeat that premise.</div> </div> </div> </div>The premise of the game and this specific book is that the Titanomachy is a war that envolves all the pantheons. That in itself is not real mythology from the start, it is an alternate mythology. <br /> <br /> My point being: complaining about a whether a non-greek god would be a Titan or not or be part of the Titanomachy or not is already debating artistic license not actual mythology since the Tiitanomachy is something that only existed in Greek mythology.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T16:57:22-07:00","id":1411592,"title":"","content":"Except it isn\u2019t? The premise of the game is playing mythology in the modern day, some pantheons even ones with Titans don\u2019t even care about the titanomachy. Sure it\u2019s the premise of this specific book but even then it still acknowledges that not every game is going to focus on the titanomachy and that not every pantheon believes in it. Also reminder part of Scion 2e\u2019s advertisement is faithfulness to mythology, so people do have a right to be miffed when it goes against that, especially since it has been faithful and accurate to the source material while still working within the game\u2019s frameworks and mechanics in other parts.<br /> <br /> As an aside I also really like the Destroyer Knack \u201cBy Will Alone\u201d genuine fingerguns are great, I also like the Monster Knack Strange Skin, shapeshifting has always been a favorite of mine in gameplay","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T17:16:35-07:00","id":1411594,"title":"","content":"Actually I\u2019m gonna expand further, I think Monster might be one of my favorite Callings right now, it\u2019s so perfect for playing a monstrous humanoid without having to make a new Denizen path. Chimera Hide and Red of Tooth and Claw are perfect for that, and Appetite for Victory is great for a berserker type character too. It\u2019s honestly getting hard to decide which one I like more, Monster or Primeval","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T17:58:23-07:00","id":1411596,"title":"","content":"Having taken a few reads through it now, I think I'm just going to ignore the whole Titans part for know and just use the Antagonists section and the rules in the Appendix in my games. I'm really liking the new Callings and the Collateral rules. The Calling work great for regular Scions that want to represent something a bit darker. I've already got ideas (so do a few of my players) for characters with the Destroyer Calling, the Monster Calling and the Primeval Calling. If you want to make a Scion heading to a God of Fear type deal, the Monster Calling will certainly work well. If you want to make a Scion heading towards a God of the Wild Untamed, the Primeval Calling will help with that.<br /> <br /> The mechanical stuff in Titanomachy looks good to me. Though I am iffy on the world lore stuff in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/898-kurasu","name":"kurasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T19:30:16-07:00","id":1411602,"title":"","content":"True enough. I had a good chortle at the Internet Literal Trolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T19:48:33-07:00","id":1411603,"title":"","content":"I'm digging a lot of the organizations and cults in the book. Saturnian Society, Starlight Solutions, and Raijin's James Bond-like super criminal organization are pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T01:28:46-07:00","id":1411618,"title":"","content":"To be honest? I'm rather shocked by the writer's attitude of going back to First Edition's approach of &quot;it's just a game, we don't have to take the myths soooo seriously&quot; and ignoring fluff AND crunch of the Second Edition's other two books (e.g. Virtues, Purviews). Some decisions are so mindboggeling weird/wrong (e.g. Nidhogg's enemy is himself spelled correctly) that I just have no words for that. I really had such high hopes for the Second Edition - and I really love the other books, even though they have their own problems -, but... Titanomachy is really underwhelming at the moment. Sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":50,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/50-blacklotos","user":"BlackLotos","date":". 09-04-2020, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/50-blacklotos","name":"BlackLotos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar50_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T03:44:13-07:00","id":1411624,"title":"","content":"Honestly I\u2019m fine with the one Purview and Titan Virtues being gone, they were always iffy, I just wish the book would outright say that. I do like Cernunoos but I do wonder why he\u2019s a Tuatha Titan when there\u2019s already so many awesome and interesting Irish Saga figures that could have been used, why couldn\u2019t Cernunoos be like an independent Titan? Why attach him to the Tuatha pantheon like this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24769,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","user":"Magicjohnny","date":". 09-03-2020, 06:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T03:54:03-07:00","id":1411625,"title":"","content":"Also I think the reason why Nidhoggr but spelled properly is enemies with Nidhoggr is because N\u00ed\u00f0h\u00f6ggr is going to be a Dragon, since he\u2019s described as one in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T04:59:17-07:00","id":1411631,"title":"","content":"There do seem to be a lot o get people sharing certain identities running around. Lots of mantles being separated from origin and being taken on by different entities.<br /> Not necessarily a bad thing.<br /> <br /> I am disappointed by the lack of mention of Titanic Virtues, but given you can't play as an actual Titan yet, they may be holding on to that for Scion: God.<br /> Still I am enjoying it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T07:07:14-07:00","id":1411635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1411631#post1411631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There do seem to be a lot o get people sharing certain identities running around. Lots of mantles being separated from origin and being taken on by different entities.<br /> Not necessarily a bad thing.<br /> <br /> I am disappointed by the lack of mention of Titanic Virtues, but given you can't play as an actual Titan yet, they may be holding on to that for Scion: God.<br /> Still I am enjoying it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And given how the second chapter mentions Virtues directly, I'm almost entirely sure that's an oversight or victim of wordcount.<br /> <br /> No worries, though. They aren't hard to junction in, and even if not, one doesn't need those Virtues to have disagreements within a pantheon, do we, Susannoo?<br /> <br /> I do feel like the Three Great Evil Yokai were missed...but I like the Kami Titans fine as is. I'm going to try and come up with a Sutoku writeup later; odds are he and Fujin are besties in suffering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T10:29:02-07:00","id":1411649,"title":"","content":"Actually I am curious about the Monster Knack Red in Claw and Fang, it says that you gain a weapon with the natural tag, and additional tags equal to your Monster Calling, I\u2019m guessing it means tag points, but does it go on top of the three points weapons have by default or does it replace that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T10:32:28-07:00","id":1411650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1411649#post1411649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I am curious about the Monster Knack Red in Claw and Fang, it says that you gain a weapon with the natural tag, and additional tags equal to your Monster Calling, I\u2019m guessing it means tag points, but does it go on top of the three points weapons have by default or does it replace that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Report that in the errata","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T10:35:42-07:00","id":1411652,"title":"","content":"I already did \ud83d\ude42","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T19:23:37-07:00","id":1411734,"title":"","content":"I did say I would write this. Fair note, I'm only using one source and the summary version on there.:<br /> <br /> <b>Sutoku-tenno, the Demon Emperor</b><br /> <br /> aka: Yamato Akihito<br /> <br /> While there are three Great Evil Yokai of Japan, each one a powerful human who somehow became a titanspawn yokai, and from there a true Titan, Sutoku is by far the most amenable to creating Scions, for the same reason he bares the unique honor among his peers of being enshrined as a Kami in his beloved Kyoto. Frankly, after everything he went through, the fact that he was still coherent enough to focus his rage on the imperial politics he was born at the apex of seemingly purely so that all ostensibly beneath him could more efficiently punch him in a very sensitive spot is commendable. Before he became the most powerful tengu ever recorded, he was indeed Emperor of Japan, and had a beloved and doting father that wanted nothing more than for his son to be a good ruler - which was a problem, because his biological father was, for all Sutoku can tell (and in truth, wants to believe) the <i>retired </i>Emperor Shirakawa, rather than the reigning Emperor Toba, a fact with his ostensible legal father never forgave him for. More than that, the unfortunate Prince Akihito was sworn in at the tender age of five, following the tradition of the court, and allowing Toba enough power and influence to unleash profound abuse on the child-Emperor until he was forced to retire early - and hand off the reins to Toba's actual son, not coincidentally - just to <i>get away </i>from it all, which Toba then happily exploited to turn Sutoku into a powerless pariah in a gilded cage, unable to even advise his younger half-brother or enjoy life away from the stifling nature of the pre-shogunate imperial court.<br /> <br /> Of course, what Toba didn't expect was that Sutoku was always the healthier and more romantically inclined of the brothers, so when Emperor Konoe died, Sutoku had his own backup heir coincidentally ready to inherit and maybe actually perform the duties of a retired emperor now that he had some experience and distance from his oppressor. Unfortunately for him, Toba had not been idle, stocking the court with his supporters and sycophants, who decided that infancy was not nearly enough of a disqualifying trait to pass the throne to Toba's fourth son, something Sutoku and the many allies he had made in his initial exile did not buy to the tune of a full-scale rebellion soon after Toba's death.<br /> <br /> What happened next, however, is what truly set Sutoku on his path to Titanic vengeance; the forces of the court, fearing that Sutoku's charisma would lead to further rebellions or worse, a valid claim, proceeded to execute not only the rebels, but their entire families for their disobedience in order to intimidate the remainder into mute obedience. While even they could not convince the executioners to harm a descendant of Amaterasu, they certainly could inform him of their fates, before all but forcing him to become a monk in a far-off monastery. When he came offering lovingly copied and decorated manuscripts to make Kyoto beautiful with and as an offering of peace, the court decreed that, since they were obviously cursed due to the person who made them, they should be destroyed, and sent back to him as ashes.<br /> <br /> Needless to say, Sutoku decided at this point that cursing the court was actually a decent suggestion. Especially the part about biting off his own tongue and making a prayer to Izanami in blood to grant him the capacity to pursue his vengeance against the system that had heaped misery and indignity upon him his whole life. She was listening, and seeing a bit of herself in the tragic emperor, granted his wish.<br /> <br /> While it was decreed by the new emperor that Sutoku would be unmourned for having been such a criminal, any attempts to dishonor his corpse proved fruitless when decay simply did not affect him; except for his de-tongued state, the cursed monk appeared to be peacefully sleeping a month later when brought to the crematorium. There, a storm that drew blood from stone heralded his arrival, and when he finally was cremated, ash the color of thunderclouds drifted in defiance of all weather to Kyoto. In less than twenty years, the entire line of Toba was rendered powerless by natural disasters and sudden rebellions inspired by a strange, regal tengu with hair like an onryo's - followed soon after by the very court itself, beginning the age of the shogun and the emperor becoming a figurehead - which much less drama attached to his life, giving him a chance for a vaguely content one.<br /> <br /> Sutoku now is a personification of the natural disasters that force traditions to adapt or die, and occupies an ambivalent spot among the Kami. On the one hand, he did more or less singlehandedly reduce the power of the emperor to a figurehead for much of Japan's existence, and only through honoring him as a Kami did the Meiji Restoration ensure that the forces of the emperor didn't singlehandedly die by sudden typhoons. At the same time, he also is a crusader against the corruption and greed that destroyed his mortal life, and he was one of the first to realize that Japan's imperial ambitions in the leadup to WWII would doom it if not curtailed. While he despises Amaterasu for what he sees as the dereliction of her duty to protect her descendants, he has little anger towards the rest of the Kami; he just finds their Titans agree with his tempestuous demeanor more, especially Fujin, who understands the nihilistic rage and sorrow he felt in the last days of his mortal life. He has no particular desire to rule again, either; he always preferred life in exile and his religious life more. Rather, he is a cheerfully radical political philosopher who falls in love with any movement that promises to liberate both the weak and the powerful from the burden of institutional rulership; he will support communist revolutionaries and libertarian uprisings in the same breath without noticing a difference, or caring. For the most part though, he seeks the faults in power structures to unleash disasters upon, eager to see if the state will thrive in the face of adversity or be torn down to build a better one. He is especially proud of the destruction of the Chernobyl reactor, and how it led to the end of the Soviet Union and the possible permanent destruction of all states that could be reformed forever.<br /> <br /> When he walks in the World, Sutoku is fully aware of how he often appears as the epitome of the troubled but handsome Byronic hero; there are more than a couple dating sims he has licensed out his favored faces and writing advice to, though his fury is spectacular should he realize his face belongs to a romantic abuser - it reminds him far too much of his past. It should come as no surprise that he has a significant portion of Born Scions, but he actually prefers Chosen for the simple reason that he has vowed to himself to never be Toba; he does not trust himself to be able to dote on too many families at once, so he only has a couple children to focus on until their adulthood at once. Naturally, the people he Chooses tend to be countercultural leaders; anarchist philosophers, artistic teachers, and master survivalists. Even more naturally, all of them are angry enough at the status quo to be willing to blow it up, secure in the belief that whatever comes next is an improvement by default.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtues:</b> Sincerity, Fecundity<br /> <br /> <b>Callings: </b>Adversary, Destroyer, Leader<br /> <br /> <b>Purviews: </b>Artistry (Writing), Beasts (Corvids), Chaos, Death, Fortune, Passion (Cold Rage), Order, Sky<br /> <br /> EDIT: Not sure if he should be a Monster instead of an Adversary, though. He's way too direct and is very much about letting you know he's there. Leader is staying, though; his major positive quality is that he is honestly a fair and even-keeled politician when he's calm. It's what makes him a patron of rebels.<br /> <br /> Still on his associations, but the major thing is that he seeks to unseat Amaterasu in the possibly accurate belief she could have saved him from his stepfather but didn't, and is happy to work with other Titans and Gods to embarrass her. He's not nearly so eager to deal with Titans who view their Scions as tools (which is why he hasn't allied with Apep into the Sun Hater Club), and his Scions are fewer compared to other Titans, but doted on; he doesn't Visit you unless he likes you, and so he encourages other potential Titans; the more storms to change the world, the better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 09-04-2020, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T01:27:49-07:00","id":1411758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1411734#post1411734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did say I would write this. Fair note, I'm only using one source and the summary version on there.:<br /> <br /> <b>Sutoku-tenno, the Demon Emperor</b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Great work, I love it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T15:39:14-07:00","id":1411912,"title":"","content":"When was the titanomachy released to the backers I must have missed that email but I will search it if I can be pointed to the date.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T15:46:26-07:00","id":1411914,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> Titanomachy wasn't part of the original kickstarter. It is its own book that was released earlier this week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/898-kurasu","name":