 Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T17:29:27-07:00","id":1411949,"title":"","content":"To be fair the book does mention that gods can have Titan Callings too if the table decide they fit more","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T17:31:15-07:00","id":1411952,"title":"","content":"Ya<br /> <br /> The murkiness of what and who is a titan is something i rather like in this edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T18:01:10-07:00","id":1411965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1411952#post1411952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ya<br /> <br /> The murkiness of what and who is a titan is something i rather like in this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah it could work with the setting and the political use of the label if Prometheus was fully a God by virtue of siding with the Olympians, but in sentencing him to eternal torment later Zeus relabeled him Titan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T19:39:56-07:00","id":1411986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1411945#post1411945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the &quot;Titans must have at least one Titan Calling&quot; rule, there really is no way for Prometheus to be one, since he absolutely needs Creator, Sage, and Trickster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure it's trickster and not Advisary which is like trickster but more focused on opposing someone than making them play the fool. Trickery can be involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T19:41:34-07:00","id":1411987,"title":"","content":"I do think &quot;Titans must have at least one Titan Calling&quot; seems inconsistent with &quot;'Titan' is just a political designation some pantheons use for their enemies to legitimize attacking them&quot; as implied by the \u00d2r\u00ecsh\u00e0/Loa section. There doesn't really need to be an objective difference between Gods and Titans IMO. Everyone should just have the Callings that suit them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T20:12:04-07:00","id":1411993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1411986#post1411986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure it's trickster and not Advisary which is like trickster but more focused on opposing someone than making them play the fool. Trickery can be involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar600_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"600\" data-vbnamecard=\"600\">HaplessWithDice</a> here - if you think that Prometheus should be Titan-Titan, he should get Adversary, not Trickster. Because Adversary Calling, really, is just 'bad Trickster' in the first place.<br /> <br /> If you want to play as 'Prometheus is God, only labelled Titan from political reasons' angle - then give him Trickster. Case closed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T22:37:06-07:00","id":1412006,"title":"","content":"Uh, what's the logic behind the whole Nidhoggr doppelg\u00e4nger thing that BlackLotos mentioned? Like, why is it a thing? Is it something to do with Dragon-stuff or something? I don't know why I find myself fixating upon it, but it just seems so-... Perplexing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","user":"Kleptomania","date":". 09-05-2020, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T23:35:09-07:00","id":1412009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412006#post1412006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh, what's the logic behind the whole Nidhoggr doppelg\u00e4nger thing that BlackLotos mentioned? Like, why is it a thing? Is it something to do with Dragon-stuff or something? I don't know why I find myself fixating upon it, but it just seems so-... Perplexing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing it's meant to pave the way for Scion: Dragon. You know, the book we were promised wouldn't be intertwined with other books. There are a few other nods to Dragon in Titanomachy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T03:15:24-07:00","id":1412035,"title":"","content":"Most of the Titan Callings have associations that can be drawn to 'normal' Callings, which can make for some easy-ish substitutions'.<ul><li>Adversary to Trickster, as pointed out above</li> <li>Destroyer to Warrior is harder, but doable.</li> <li>Monster shares more with Hunter than I thought, but is easiest the weakest link among the associations.</li> <li>Tyrant to Leader, obviously.</li> </ul><br /> Primeval has no equivalent.<br /> <br /> So if one needs too, we have some options to 'godify' or 'titanify' entities.<br /> As for Prometheus...the sample born scion of his in the adversary section (NOT THE MARRIED COUPLE) kinda implies a recent Mantle change. From a peace advocate who disappears for years to take care of 'family matters' to someone who shows up to conscript his own child into a war. And if Mantles are in play, there maybe a God Prometheus and a Titan Prometheus, who could even be the same person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":".  Autocorrect turned primeval into primordial, fixinyg 09-05-2020, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T03:57:12-07:00","id":1412045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412009#post1412009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm guessing it's meant to pave the way for Scion: Dragon. You know, the book we were promised wouldn't be intertwined with other books. There are a few other nods to Dragon in Titanomachy.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Umlaute seem to be funny, even though they are used in the original sources. Which, as a German, is... a little bit off-putting. Making the English spelling the true one somehow.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/50-blacklotos","name":"BlackLotos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar50_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T04:00:34-07:00","id":1412046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412035#post1412035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the Titan Callings have associations that can be drawn to 'normal' Callings, which can make for some easy-ish substitutions'.<ul><li>Adversary to Trickster, as pointed out above</li> <li>Destroyer to Warrior is harder, but doable.</li> <li>Monster shares more with Hunter than I thought, but is easiest the weakest link among the associations.</li> <li>Tyrant to Leader, obviously.</li> </ul><br /> Primordial has no equivalent.<br /> <br /> So if one needs too, we have some options to 'godify' or 'titanify' entities.<br /> As for Prometheus...the sample born scion of his in the adversary section (NOT THE MARRIED COUPLE) kinda implies a recent Mantle change. From a peace advocate who disappears for years to take care of 'family matters' to someone who shows up to conscript his own child into a war. And if Mantles are in play, there maybe a God Prometheus and a Titan Prometheus, who could even be the same person.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then I ask myself: why not fold the &quot;good&quot; and the &quot;evil&quot; Calling into one, which allows the Gods and Titans to be on one scale which is neither good nor evil? For example: some beings have more Knacks which are Tyrant now, some have more Knacks which are Leader now. But all of them represent leading. Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":50,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/50-blacklotos","user":"BlackLotos","date":". 09-05-2020, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/50-blacklotos","name":"BlackLotos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar50_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T04:52:44-07:00","id":1412051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlackLotos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412046#post1412046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But then I ask myself: why not fold the &quot;good&quot; and the &quot;evil&quot; Calling into one, which allows the Gods and Titans to be on one scale which is neither good nor evil? For example: some beeings have more Knacks which are Tyrant now, some have more Knacks which are Leader now. But all of them represent leading. Just a thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the looking for correspondences thing is not helpful for making these Callings actually <i>work</i>. Rather, one should invest that thought into how they are distinct from the already existing Callings. I still haven't taken time to read that section thoroughly yet (I have been hung up on my discontents with the Pantheon-specific sections), but my surface-level impression of the mechanics is favorable. Destroyer, Monster, and Adversary all seem like good design options for me to flesh out not just Titans, but also Gods like Shiva or Sobek and of course their potential Scions, too. A lot of what is now contained in Titanic Callings until now overburdened existing Callings, specifically Liminal, which has to take care of underworld people, travelers, and all manner of outsiders. A lot of antisocial figures can now be expressed more specifically, I like that. It makes for powers that fit individual characters better. I agree, however, that Tyrant is the most difficult to distinguish from an earlier counterpart, namely Leader. Conceptually, I'm playing with analogies like &quot;Leader is rule through charisma, competence, divine right, etc., Tyrant is rule through usurpation and force,&quot; but I'm not quite happy with that yet either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T05:56:53-07:00","id":1412060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412009#post1412009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm guessing it's meant to pave the way for Scion: Dragon. You know, the book we were promised wouldn't be intertwined with other books. There are a few other nods to Dragon in Titanomachy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The great thing about setting books is that Storyguides (and their players) can still decide whether or not they want to include references to other books. You are free to completely ignore the Nidhoggr doppleganger all together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.erykahfassett.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman, serif\"><b>Erykah Fassett</b></span></a><br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;The closer you get to the light, the greater your shadow becomes.&quot;</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24398-shadowblossoms","name":"ShadowBlossoms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24398_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T05:57:35-07:00","id":1412061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlackLotos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412045#post1412045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And Umlaute seem to be funny, even though they are used in the original sources. Which, as a German, is... a little bit off-putting. Making the English spelling the true one somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Release schedules not necessarily lining up with the order things are outlined/contracted/written in sometimes determine which spelling got used first. It's really not any deeper than that. <br /> <br /> Neither Nidhoggr or N\u00ed\u0111h\u00f6ggr are more &quot;real&quot; than one other in a chronicle that's using Dragon once it's out, and if you're not, then that sentence is irrelevant anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25521-spider","name":"Spider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25521_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T06:16:30-07:00","id":1412062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlackLotos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412046#post1412046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But then I ask myself: why not fold the &quot;good&quot; and the &quot;evil&quot; Calling into one, which allows the Gods and Titans to be on one scale which is neither good nor evil? For example: some beeings have more Knacks which are Tyrant now, some have more Knacks which are Leader now. But all of them represent leading. Just a thought.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10624_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10624\" data-vbnamecard=\"10624\">Sacerdos</a> is following the same line of logic I am here. The idea I had with the parallel Callings is provide ideas for alternate Mantles. Heck two of the sample Tuatha De Domnu Titans ARE Nementondevos deities. Even this book plays a little loose with definition of Titan. Remember, Callings are an out-of-game concept, unlike Purviews. Gods don't technically know about Callings, though it is naive to say they haven't noticed certain behaviour groupings. The Titan Callings are a bit more removed from a healthy human mindset (much like Titanic Virtues), which is one of the indicators I assume the more scholarly deities use to identify Titans.<br /> <br /> Mind you Titanmachy appears to focus on the Titans that want to oppose the Gods, without erasing more...passive Titans. Danu certainly has a Primeval Calling in one of Mantles, Shiva has got to have a mantle with Destroyer Calling somewhen/where. Neither are considered Titans. Even with these new Callings, 'Titan' is a political term. It is just Gods can spot behaviours associated with these Callings; they know not to get too close to an Adversary, they worry about protecting their things/people/etc from Destroyers, recognise the disassociation that occurs with the Primeval Calling, they abhor Tyrants and as for Monsters...well, many Heroes make their names through monster-slaying.<br /> <br /> I DO think there SHOULD be Titans without one of the new Callings. But that is such a minor issue, I'm not planning on reporting it as an inconsistency; I'm content to house rule it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 09-05-2020, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T06:37:25-07:00","id":1412064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412061#post1412061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Release schedules not necessarily lining up with the order things are outlined/contracted/written in sometimes determine which spelling got used first. It's really not any deeper than that.<br /> <br /> Neither Nidhoggr or N\u00ed\u0111h\u00f6ggr are more &quot;real&quot; than one other in a chronicle that's using Dragon once it's out, and if you're not, then that sentence is irrelevant anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why was it decided this figure needed a spelling difference for splitting, but e.g. Cernunnos didn't? Is there deeper meaning to that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T06:37:33-07:00","id":1412065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412009#post1412009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm guessing it's meant to pave the way for Scion: Dragon. You know, the book we were promised wouldn't be intertwined with other books. There are a few other nods to Dragon in Titanomachy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can guarantee you that there are zero promises about Dragon &quot;not being intertwined with other books&quot; only the assurance that with all things, if you do not want to use it at your table, you certainly don't have to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Danielle Lauzon, Requiem Developer, Storypath Guru, freelance writer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6155-impernious","name":"impernious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T06:41:28-07:00","id":1412067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowBlossoms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412060#post1412060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The great thing about setting books is that Storyguides (and their players) can still decide whether or not they want to include references to other books. You are free to completely ignore the Nidhoggr doppleganger all together.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is absolutely true! Basically anything anyone disagrees with can be houseruled away, 1e has taught us that much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I was more talking about how there were assurance on the part of Neall and other Devs back when these books were announced and that people put their money in these books trusting that what would be in them would be what had been promised. And I think it's fair to point out where such assurances and promises have been broken, because the loss of trust in the product and its developers that may cause <i>cannot</i> simply be houseruled away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T06:44:41-07:00","id":1412068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>impernious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412065#post1412065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can guarantee you that there are zero promises about Dragon &quot;not being intertwined with other books&quot; only the assurance that with all things, if you do not want to use it at your table, you certainly don't have to.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that is the new status quo of development, I will of course have to accept that. I was merely speaking of what <i>was</i>, not what <i>is</i>. But thank you for confirmation on where things stand at now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T06:56:23-07:00","id":1412070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412064#post1412064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why was it decided this figure needed a spelling difference for splitting, but e.g. Cernunnos didn't? Is there deeper meaning to that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most Titans and dragons have multiple names and Mantles, making it possible for a Storyguide to assign one variant to a Titan and one to a dragon, at least in out-of-game conversation. Referring to the dragon only as Apep, and the Titan only as Apophis, makes it immediately clear to which entity the Storyguide refers when she says, \u201cApep\u2019s followers were responsible for that bombing last session, remember?\u201d <br /> For those Titans and dragons who have only one name and no Mantles but exist on both sides of the aisle, Storyguides may wish to assign a color signifier, or simply make it explicit to which entity they refer by calling them \u201cThe Dragon [Name]\u201d and \u201cThe Titan [Name].\u201d </div> </div> </div>Titanomachy, pp 80-81<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25521-spider","name":"Spider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25521_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T07:01:33-07:00","id":1412071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412070#post1412070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Titanomachy, pp 80-81</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thank you. I should have connected the dots on that one.So it's a Dragon-specific thing. Curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T07:07:14-07:00","id":1412074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412071#post1412071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, thank you. I should have connected the dots on that one.So it's a Dragon-specific thing. Curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a thing where I wrote all of the pieces you're asking about (save the non-Titan Cernnunos) and followed my own advice about how to draw easily-understood distinctions in text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25521-spider","name":"Spider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25521_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T07:08:53-07:00","id":1412075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412074#post1412074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a thing where I wrote all of the pieces you're asking about (save the non-Titan Cernnunos) and followed my own advice about how to draw easily-understood distinctions in text.</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked about one thing, and am honestly baffled by the mocking tone you're now taking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T07:16:10-07:00","id":1412077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412075#post1412075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I asked about one thing, and am honestly baffled by the mocking tone you're now taking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not. I'm clarifying, solely and only, because I don't want anything read into what I said that isn't there. There is no hidden meaning behind the decision to differentiate one thing and not the other; it's a function of 'One person wrote these four parts across these two books, but not this fifth part in a third book, so the four parts that were written by one person across two books follow the advice written in the advice-giving bit of one of those books, while that fifth part written in a third book by someone else does not follow that differentiation-in-spelling convention.'<br /> <br /> There is no mocking tone, and there is no hidden meaning. You asked a question, I answered it. That's all there is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25521,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25521-spider","user":"Spider","date":". 09-05-2020, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25521-spider","name":"Spider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25521_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T07:28:21-07:00","id":1412081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412077#post1412077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not. I'm clarifying, solely and only, because I don't want anything read into what I said that isn't there. There is no hidden meaning behind the decision to differentiate one thing and not the other; it's a function of 'One person wrote these four parts across these two books, but not this fifth part in a third book, so the four parts that were written by one person across two books follow the advice written in that book, while that fifth part written in a third book by someone else does not follow that differentiation-in-spelling convention.'<br /> <br /> There is no mocking tone, and there is no hidden meaning. You asked a question, I answered it. That's all there is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry you feel put under pressure like that. I can't speak for others, but I don't go out of my way to misunderstand people on purpose. I guess what you intended to be a cautious reply just came across as sarcastic to me. I apologise for misconstruing your intention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T12:50:14-07:00","id":1412143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412061#post1412061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Release schedules not necessarily lining up with the order things are outlined/contracted/written in sometimes determine which spelling got used first. It's really not any deeper than that.<br /> <br /> Neither Nidhoggr or N\u00ed\u0111h\u00f6ggr are more &quot;real&quot; than one other in a chronicle that's using Dragon once it's out, and if you're not, then that sentence is irrelevant anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>But... which language is Nidhoggr's first/preferred language that it makes a statement like &quot;Just look at those umlauts and accents in his name, written properly as the Sagas demand!&quot;? It has to be some language without Umlaute.<br /> And has N\u00ed\u0111h\u00f6ggr a name tag or writes signed letters a lot that it matters that there are dots above the o?<br /> Because if both statements are not true, then it doesn't matter that N\u00ed\u0111h\u00f6ggr has Umlaute in its name.<br /> <br /> You make a very English-centric statement. And an insensitive one at that, I think.<br /> <br /> And why do you fabricate a problem with the doppleganger instead of using the already existing one (eagle - Ratatoskr - N\u00ed\u0111h\u00f6ggr), which, I think, is a perfect seed for conflict, and building on that? Was the myth not interesting enough for you?<br /> <br /> But all in all that's sadly just the tip of the iceberg, only one of the ideas that are not really thought through. Some chapters are nice like the Orisha and Deva ones, but others are just... First Edition fantasy fabrications which have nothing to do with the myths. And that's not what the 2nd Edition game line was advertised as.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":50,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/50-blacklotos","user":"BlackLotos","date":". 09-05-2020, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/50-blacklotos","name":"BlackLotos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar50_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T16:22:53-07:00","id":1412180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlackLotos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412143#post1412143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But... which language is Nidhoggr's first/preferred language that it makes a statement like &amp;quot;Just look at those umlauts and accents in his name, written properly as the Sagas demand!&amp;quot;? It has to be some language without Umlaute.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nidhoggr is a Titan. N\u00ed\u0111h\u00f6ggr is a dragon. What's the native language of immortal beings who precede all human thought?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachme