nd of thing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 09-05-2020, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T20:06:12-07:00","id":1412206,"title":"","content":"Anyone have any ideas for which Purviews are THE purview of these newly introduce Titans? I'm not sure if they all should get one, but certainly the less blurry cases should lean that way.<br /> Or which Virtues they may have? Titanic Virtues are based around a particular Purview, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T20:09:44-07:00","id":1412209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412206#post1412206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone have any ideas for which Purviews are THE purview of these newly introduce Titans? I'm not sure if they all should get one, but certainly the less blurry cases should lean that way.<br /> Or which Virtues they may have? Titanic Virtues are based around a particular Purview, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the virtues were removed or whatever they aren't really covered. As for purviews we had stuff like Tyrant, destroyer, and monster for titanic purviews.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T20:17:03-07:00","id":1412211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412209#post1412209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the virtues were removed or whatever they aren't really covered. As for purviews we had stuff like Tyrant, destroyer, and monster for titanic purviews.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are Titanic Callings, not Purviews. Titans have the same Purviews as Gods, but what separates them is having at least 1 Calling that is 'Titanic'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/898-kurasu","name":"kurasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T20:20:51-07:00","id":1412213,"title":"","content":"Yeah, although even that\u2019s loose since the book outright says that plenty of gods have those too. Like there\u2019s pretty much no way Shiva doesn\u2019t have Destroyer for example, or any of the Theoi not having Primeval","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T20:38:04-07:00","id":1412214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412213#post1412213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, although even that\u2019s loose since the book outright says that plenty of gods have those too. Like there\u2019s pretty much no way Shiva doesn\u2019t have Destroyer for example, or any of the Theoi not having Primeval</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very true, but the book specifically states, on page 13, first sentence of the second paragraph, &quot;A Titan must have a Titanic Calling: Adversary, Destroyer, Monster, Primeval, or Tyrant.&quot; Not all beings with a Titanic Calling are Titans, but all Titans have a Titanic Calling. Also in the book, it says that while Gods can have Mantles with the Titanic Callings, other Gods look at those Mantles with distrust or fear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":898,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/898-kurasu","user":"kurasu","date":". 09-05-2020, 11:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/898-kurasu","name":"kurasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T21:11:03-07:00","id":1412215,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering if a possible generic definition of Titan (as opposed to the original Theoi meaning) might be a deity who is in some way hostile to either the Pantheon or to their worshipers. At least that seems to be a commonality with the five Titan callings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T22:19:59-07:00","id":1412219,"title":"","content":"There is direct pointing in Demigod Preview 1 about Demigods taking Titan Callings - <br /> 'Titans on the Threshold<br /> While completing the Threshold Deed, a Demigod can choose to take on any of the Titanic Callings from Titanomachy as part of his progress. If he still has any of those Callings when he completes the Milestone, however, it becomes a fixed part of his character and will cause other legendary beings to treat him accordingly.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T23:05:16-07:00","id":1412223,"title":"","content":"Honestly given that most of the rules seem to have exceptions (There are many Gods who have Titanic Callings, for instance), I may just take the mechanics of Titanomachy and just go &quot;Okay so, the Titan-God Divide is basically political. Here are the Callings. There's sixteen of them... Or fifteen and a half if you can sweet-talk me into making the Tyrant Knacks be Jackass Leader Knacks.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T00:29:09-07:00","id":1412230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412223#post1412223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly given that most of the rules seem to have exceptions (There are many Gods who have Titanic Callings, for instance), I may just take the mechanics of Titanomachy and just go &quot;Okay so, the Titan-God Divide is basically political. Here are the Callings. There's sixteen of them... Or fifteen and a half if you can sweet-talk me into making the Tyrant Knacks be Jackass Leader Knacks.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you've gone and made me want a Calling of Magnificent Bastard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T02:27:40-07:00","id":1412237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412230#post1412230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now you've gone and made me want a Calling of Magnificent Bastard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is Adversary, Trickster, and Tyrant combined...if you are a real Bas*@$$d. Drop Tyrant and pick up Lover if you have a heart of gold.<br /> I may be playing around with some concepts, sorry.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T05:05:13-07:00","id":1412260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412230#post1412230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now you've gone and made me want a Calling of Magnificent Bastard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I want the Magnificent Bastard calling too! What a Great idea No One of Consequence!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T06:33:38-07:00","id":1412269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1412223#post1412223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly given that most of the rules seem to have exceptions (There are many Gods who have Titanic Callings, for instance), I may just take the mechanics of Titanomachy and just go &quot;Okay so, the Titan-God Divide is basically political. Here are the Callings. There's sixteen of them... Or fifteen and a half if you can sweet-talk me into making the Tyrant Knacks be Jackass Leader Knacks.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly what I'm doing in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/898-kurasu","name":"kurasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-12T10:31:21-07:00","id":1413251,"title":"","content":"So, I have sat on Titanomachy and tried to figure out what isnt sitting right with me.<br /> <br /> Warning -- a bit ranty --<br /> <br /> I'm really hoping the development team does another major pass on this book. Titanomachy feels like it could be a lot more sophisticated (and probably should be, considering the material).<br /> <br /> My biggest issue is that it doent do a lot to define the nature and motivations of the Titans writ large (outside of the new Callings, which dont get a lot of attention or discussion). &quot;Titanism&quot; seems to basically be a term of ostracism or a political decision - but why? I really want a LOT more wordcount on what makes a Titan a Titan and why they are a threat that requires a &quot;cold war.&quot; Id like more exploration on their motivations and relationship to humanity... because right now, as bad guys and challenges? They fall flat. If anything, many of the Titans are outright sympathetic rather than nuanced antagonists.<br /> <br /> The reader is expected to simply accept the imperative to fight the Titans because they have been ostracized and labeled them as the &quot;other&quot; by the Gods (that in itself is a bit troubling). Titanomachy doesnt give us a sense of the need or reason to oppose the Titans -- especially when we see time and again that the Titans are basically the Gods-but-not. A few examples of the havoc or destruction the Titans have wrought would be helpful as well. I want to know the consequences if my PC scion doesnt fight against the machinations of the Titans.<br /> <br /> Titanomachy's entries on the various Titans is super useful -- but if we dont know what binds the Titans (across pantheons) then we dont have an understanding of the nature of the conflict. This really irks me because this was THE major failing of 1e in my opinion. In 1e the Titans were described as bad guys, but rarely explored.<br /> <br /> Likewise, how many Titans do we have that are various iterations of &quot;they want to be the Joker and watch the world burn.&quot; Okay. But why? Scion's modern takes on the Gods (and Titans) is a great opportunity to explore modern sensibilities and philosophy in terms of villains. I want more than just motorcycles as stand-ins for horses and guns as stand-ins for axes. I want to see more discussion of the modern vs ancient and how that impacts the Titans -- especially as that sort of disconnect could be a really cool motivator.** Instead of wordcount dedicated to stories I can pull off of wikipedia, give me something I cant find on the web. Help me understand what makes the various Titans tick in the modern world and how their old school motivations interact with modern sensibilities. <i><b>That </b></i>would be super interesting and useful.<br /> <br /> I really hope the Dev team cuts about 10k words from the generic parts of the antagonist section and applies that wordcount to talking about <i>who </i>and <i>what </i>the Titans are. Help the players and Storyguide to understand why there is a driving imperative to oppose the Titans. Tell us what makes a Titan a Titan. Tell us why a cold war is necessary (especially as the Titans as presented are disorganized and hardly feel like a legitimate threat to the established pantheons)... and why a hot war may be devastating.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the listing of antagonists really needs to be organized better. Throwing Titanspawn, Titan-aligned Scions, nemeses, and assorted and other sundry entries in alphabetical order isnt terribly handy. If a Storyguide wants to quickly pull up an antagonist in a game.. this is going to be too obtuse. Alphabetized entries leads to Wendigos and Nipah\u00e2hkatosow in different areas with no clear connection. Considering one is an extension of the other, I think the alphabetized entries needs to be dropped. <br /> <br /> Reorganize into types of antagonists. It would also be super helpful to have each antagonist's pantheon listed. Knowing their home region would also be helpful. I speak five different languages, have lived around the world, and am pretty well educated in the legends of the regions I have lived in... and even then there are a lot of entries I couldnt place.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> **were it me working on defining the nature of the Titans, I would riff off the disconnect between the old and the new. Titans would be the Gods/Ancient Entities who reject the modern world humanity built (and, by consequence, much of humanity). They are artifacts of a bygone era, with thinking that is so old as to basically be alien and largely incomprehensible to modern humans and the Gods of the pantheons. This divergent thinking makes them ihostile to a world and reality that clearly rejects their vision. In turn, Titans reject modernity, and each seeks to rebuke the modern world in some fashion (either actively or passively). All Titans see the Gods as sellouts and are, ultimately, resentful of the Gods' relative success.<br /> <br /> Take something like the above, give it 5k words to explore, and suddenly the Titans are worthy foes that <i><b>need </b></i>to be opposed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaponized Ink: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/288291/Werewolf-The-Savage-Age-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: The Savage Age!</a> </span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":11548,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","user":"Coyoteintx","date":". 09-12-2020, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","name":"Coyoteintx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11548_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-12T11:02:39-07:00","id":1413255,"title":"","content":"But mor than once, Neall said part of the story related to the Titans are exactly around the fact that Titans and Gods are not different from each other except for political/POV definitions, and how the characters may see Titans as equals or at least not enemies, while the only reason to treat them as enemies are the gods speech on how they are evil.<br /> <br /> Titanomachy is an antagonist book, but it\u2019s not a simple list of enemies, you can use them as enemies or allies, and most Titans are described as neutral if not apathetical to the gods and the war itself. The first time I read the Keepers plans I read them as the allies we need, not as enemies, I discovered they are supposed to be the enemies much latter, and I really enjoyed the idea of this controversial enemies.<br /> <br /> If you want them to be your enemy make them your enemy, if you want them to be a bunch of gods that don\u2019t care about people, just make them this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-12T11:27:09-07:00","id":1413260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1413255#post1413255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But mor than once, Neall said part of the story related to the Titans are exactly around the fact that Titans and Gods are not different from each other except for political/POV definitions, and how the characters may see Titans as equals or at least not enemies, while the only reason to treat them as enemies are the gods speech on how they are evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a division between &quot;God&quot; and &quot;Titan&quot; -- but Titanomachy doesnt do a terribly good job of showing us that distinction.<br /> <br /> If they are basically the same -- then I think more effort needs to be made to define what &quot;Titan&quot; means (because it clearly means <b><i>something</i></b>). If it is only a political/POV term, lets get into the nature of that politicking so we can see what it really means to be called a &quot;Titan.&quot; I would like to see some examples of how the term is applied and the implications. I'd like to see if the application of the term &quot;Titan&quot; is deserved or not depending on the recipient and the way the Pantheon approaches the term. That, I think, would be a great entry in each of the Pantheon entries -- how does each Pantheon approach the term?<br /> <br /> If it really is a political term, why is that? Is it a term of ostracism? Do some pantheons have formal rites to label a once-god a Titan? Likewise, if all it is is a political term, then why is there a mechanical division in terms of Callings?<br /> <br /> I'd like to see how those politics work and how those sort of definitions lead to the creation of a &quot;Titan.&quot; What happens when a God is labeled as such? I would assume that its not willingly accepted in many cases.<br /> <br /> ...and if Titans are just as likely to be allies or opt-out of Godly politics -- then where does the &quot;cold war&quot; theme come from? You need antagonists of relatively equal power to create a cold war. Its a theme that comes up throughout the core books and Titanomachy, but, as presented, most of the Titans in Titanomachy arent actually interested in a cold war (and certainly arent organized enough to put up a fight against the pantheons). So, the leaves us with a one-sided conflict (and, perhaps, a bit too much nuance).<br /> <br /> Also, if the Titans are meant to be allies as much as enemies -- why call the book &quot;Titanomachy?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaponized Ink: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/288291/Werewolf-The-Savage-Age-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: The Savage Age!</a> </span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":11548,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","user":"Coyoteintx","date":". 09-12-2020, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","name":"Coyoteintx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11548_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-12T16:38:50-07:00","id":1413292,"title":"","content":"Problem with term 'Titan' itself, it's that it's artificial leftover from 1E that was very Theoi oriented. And now each Pantheon 'needs' Titans - only most mythologies do not work that way like in Theoi model. Like Shen basically co-ops their 'Titans' and used them like primitive gods-servants of Greater Good. Not very Cold War here.<br /> <br /> As a gameline with 15+ various cultural factions ( Pantheons) that each works differently, I understand why authors need to be vague with the term - and then, with game material on them. It's effect of multiculturalism of the books - simple as that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-13-2020, 04:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-12T18:14:32-07:00","id":1413309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1413292#post1413292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem with term 'Titan' itself, it's that it's artificial leftover from 1E that was very Theoi oriented. And now each Pantheon 'needs' Titans - only most mythologies do not worh that way like in Theoi model. Like Shen basiclly co-ops their 'Titans' and used them like primitive gods-servants of Greater Good. Not very Cold War here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the Theoi don't really work like the Titans in Scion do.<br /> <br /> The Kronos was overthrown and defeated, the Gigantes got close but they were also defeated and destroyed, Typhon to his credit did manage to overthrow Olympus even if he failed to stick the landing. Gaia, who has played kingmaker for the position of Lord of Cosmos pretty much since there was a cosmos to be lord of is still at large and probably still plotting to overthrow Zeus, but she tends to stick backstage. They don't really have an enemy to be having a Cold War with and the ones they did defeat pretty much stay in their cages or underneath the islands that the gods threw at them.<br /> <br /> Mythologically speaking, Cold Wars don't tend to be a thing. Cyclical battles, like Re(and the rest of his dudes) vs Apep or Huitzilopochtli vs Coyolx\u0101uhqui are far more common things, along with great and terrible entities the gods defeated long ago and who's corpse they may have made the world out of.<br /> <br /> The closest thing to Cold War style Titanomachy, AFAIK, is Ragnarok wherein the Aesir and the Jotunn are destined to fight at the end and kill each other but aren't &quot;currently&quot; at war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-12T19:07:48-07:00","id":1413314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coyoteintx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1413260#post1413260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they are basically the same -- then I think more effort needs to be made to define what &quot;Titan&quot; means (because it clearly means <b><i>something</i></b>). If it is only a political/POV term, lets get into the nature of that politicking so we can see what it really means to be called a &quot;Titan.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak for any of the other writers, but I tried to frame that in my intro, for each of the things I wrote -- and it's called out specifically in a sidebar. The only real difference between the Danann and the Domnann is which matriarch they owe their declared allegiance to, which sometimes corresponds to things which were written centuries ago, and sometimes doesn't, because said matriarch has been actively recruiting for the last several centuries, giving people who didn't otherwise have a pantheon 'home' a place to land. (See: the first paragraph of Belenus.) It's in the first two sentences of the pantheon writeup, and the sidebar clarifying the names.<br /> <br /> The particular individuals chosen for the Aesir Titans are the ones who were actively harmed (or misrepresented, in the case of Surtr) by the Gods, with the exception of Nidhoggr, who I chose to represent as an example of a Monster Titan, and a head-tip to Dragon, which people can use or not use. (I wrote my bits on Dragon before I wrote this, but release schedules are what they are.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That, I think, would be a great entry in each of the Pantheon entries -- how does each Pantheon approach the term? </div> </div> </div>As I read it, the introductions to each section explain that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reorganize into types of antagonists. </div> </div> </div>This is a great suggestion and should probably go into the errata form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25521,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25521-spider","user":"Spider","date":". 09-12-2020, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25521-spider","name":"Spider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25521_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-12T20:14:31-07:00","id":1413320,"title":"","content":"My own impression - with the caveat that I've not read Titanomachy's first draft (vision issues make it problematic for me to read pdfs/screen text over a certain short length) - is that the generic basis for being a Titan in Scion is that the being in question is in some way hostile to the current Pantheon and/or humanity in general. The Netjer's &quot;Titans&quot;, for example, include the very antithesis of Ma'at, the thing that tries to eat the sun every night, and the god that tried to make himself the sole member of the pantheon. With the Deva and Manitou, their Titans in Hero are both colossal jerks who hate the rest of the pantheon and cause problems for humankind. In contrast, the Azure Dragon of the East just hates the rest of the Shen because they have constantly acted like jerks to him for as long as he can remember. (And that honestly just makes makes me want to do a game where the PCs have to get something from his palace and confuse him by showing up and actually being polite and respectful.) But again, this is just my impression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-12T21:43:44-07:00","id":1413330,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I've got to admit that the lack of definition about what a Titan is makes things a lot harder than they need to be.<br /> <br /> Like originally they were supposed to be divine beings consumed by or wholly dominated by their Purview, but now there are Titans with multiple Purviews.<br /> <br /> Then there's the Titanic Callings which could be a defining feature of the Titans except that as soon we got Titanic Callings we also got a list of Gods who also have those Callings and I wonder why they were even called &quot;Titanic&quot; to begin with. Not helped by the fact that Titans also have the original Callings.<br /> <br /> They should still have Titanic Virtues(Fecundity, Rapacity, Dominance, and Submission), but I'm not sure if those are going to be staying.<br /> <br /> <br /> At this point, I'm not sure what a Titan is supposed to be in the context of Scion. Are they supposed to be guys like Apep or the Tzitzimime who pretty much want to eat/destroy vital things like the Sun and follow that up with a planet wide death orgy? Are they supposed to be more generally the Enemies of the Gods like the Aesir with the Jotunn and with obvious conflicts like the Yazata and the Deva?<br /> <br /> In the Demigod previews, the Atua were supposed reject the distinction between God and Titan and &quot;embody that rejection&quot;, but what even is a Titan supposed to be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-12T23:07:54-07:00","id":1413333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nervaqus987</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1413330#post1413330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They should still have Titanic Virtues(Fecundity, Rapacity, Dominance, and Submission), but I'm not sure if those are going to be staying.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I picked up Titanomachy, I assumed that this was the new paradigm for Titans going forward, now that Titanic Scions were playable: no more Titanic Virtues, now they\u2019re just defined by Titanic Callings and pantheon opposition.<br /> <br /> And then Demigod\u2019s manuscript drops with all the Titans mentioned in the Pantheon writeups using the Virtue system, which both makes Titanomachy the odd one out and makes them not playable for Titanic Scions in the way that Titanomachy makes its Titans valid.<br /> <br /> Our options, generally, are as follows:<br /> <br /> #1: Leave things as they are. Titanomachy is the odd book out that defines Titans through callings and purviews, all the other books in the line define them through one (1) purview and virtues.<br /> <br /> #1a: Origin/Hero/Demigod/God define Titans by Virtues. All other books define Titans by Callings. Chaos reigns.<br /> <br /> #2: Edits are made to Titanomachy to include Titanic Virtues for the Titans therein, Titans are defined by deviation from their Pantheon\u2019s virtues.<br /> <br /> #3: Edits are made to Demigod to tweak the Titans therein to be more like Titanomachy, we now define Titans by Titanic Callings.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think the best option is #2, because that aligns Titanomachy with the books that have previously been released while still building on them, despite the fact that in a world where the Scion writers are only writing for me they\u2019d switch to Callings as the mark of Titanhood.<br /> <br /> (In this world, there\u2019s also a sidebar about Tamamo-no-Mae, Daji\u2019s infamous Japanese mantle who even tangled with the Devas, in the Shen writeup, or at the very least a shoutout to her somewhere.)<br /> <br /> #1 is, unfortunately, probably the most likely, given wordcount and production deadlines, as unsatisfying as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12958-raz_fox","name":"Raz_Fox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T00:34:43-07:00","id":1413340,"title":"","content":"I think 3 would be the worst option personally since both Titanomachy and the Demigod previews outright say gods can have Titan Callings and indeed the previews even give some to members of the more hawkish pantheons, so defining Titans by Calling would be odd. But honestly my personal best case is that there ends up being no mechanical differences between Gods and Titans, the difference is purely narrative or pantheon dependent, cause it\u2019s a lot harder for things to be ambiguous like some of the text says and implies if there is in fact meaningful differences between Gods and Titans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24769,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","user":"Magicjohnny","date":". 09-13-2020, 03:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T04:20:28-07:00","id":1413358,"title":"","content":"I would not rule out Titianic Virtues out just yet, as they are used as a major indicator of Titan behaviour towards behaviour and negotiations in the Titanomachy book itself...despite the new Titans lacking listed Virtues and an attached Purview.<br /> I assume that the Purview connected to a Titanic Virtue is this 'dominant Purview' that is teased in Demigod, but that preview is as of yet, unreleased. Furthermore, the denizen book (&quot;Saints and Monsters&quot; iirc) is called out in the first Demigod preview as having the rules for Titan Scions, so we don't even have all of that yet.<br /> <br /> As for what 'makes a Titan'; one of the points made throughout 2nd edition, is that it is primarily political, though the behaviour of Titans does follow a general trend of being more removed from the human experience, humanities concerns and to a lesser degree, less empathic in general.<br /> The Adversary &amp; Tyrant Callings strike me as particularly sociopathic. I'm not saying that having one makes you psychotic, just that other people's needs are a lower priority for you if you have one of these as the foundation of your identity.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, Adversary does require a certain degree of caring for others; it just does it in a &quot;f@#$ you&quot; kind of way.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: By contrast,the Primeval Calling is more about transcendence and being phenomena, so it is not exactly good for relating to things that aren't aspects of reality, ie Purviews. I think Helios has this Calling, and that is why he forgets that the sun can harm the mortals he interacts with occasionally.<br /> Likewise Monster is very much about being non-human and having quasi-animalistic traits. The condition that comes with the Calling reminds me of how Denizens are meant to separate themselves from humanity, so this Calling comes off as the most empathic...even if the Monstrous Urge is to trying make you eat people.<br /> <br /> It should be noted that Titanomachy isn't a book about most of the Titans, but the ones that are the most organized, active opposition to the Hero book pantheons. These are the people on the other side of the cold war. There is a reason Rhea, Nezumo and Elatha aren't in this book.<br /> While two of those people are on good terms with their pantheons, Nezumo is one I called out because (as far as i can tell) it isn't ACTIVELY hostile, rather it only accidentally causes problems while following it's Virtues (Fcundity and Submission - Earth) and it's Monster calling. He just is, and sometimes people get in his way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 09-13-2020, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T05:32:29-07:00","id":1413363,"title":"","content":"I know who Rhea is (the mother of Zeus who saved him from being eaten by Cronus). And Nezumo sounds like a Kami Titan. Who is Elatha and what pantheon is she from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T05:38:08-07:00","id":1413364,"title":"","content":"A clarification on the Virtues and why Titans are represented with only one Purview in other books but several here would be very welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T05:57:09-07:00","id":1413365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1413363#post1413363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who is Elatha and what pantheon is she from?</div> </div> </div> </div>Elatha is the father of the TDD Titan, Bres (as well as Ogma and the Dagda). By all accounts, he seems like a perfectly reasonable Fomorian: when Bres loses kingship of the TDD and scurries back home, Elatha bluntly tells him he was a bad king. He still tells Bres how to raise an army to take Ireland back, but he's obviously disappointed in his kid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T07:47:29-07:00","id":1413372,"title":"","content":"I wasn't a huge fan of the Titan Virtues, TBH. Like, they fit the paradigm of the 1e Virtues, less so in 2e. As I mentioned upthread, if I were rewriting Scion I'd probably say that 'Titan' sometimes gets used as a term for 'Enemies of the Gods' but it's frankly almost entirely a political division. They may have a primary Purview that influences them, but really I'd lean in on 'There is no clear universal God/Titan divide, some Pantheons just have really clear enemies'<br /> <br /> Assuming I even use 'Titan' as a term in my hypothetical Scion rewrite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T08:03:00-07:00","id":1413374,"title":"","content":"Okay, let's do this. I got my hard copy out for referencing purposes.<ul><li>Nezumo is found on page 79 of the Hero book.</li> <li>Rhea is listed on page 151 of Book 2: Hero.</li> <li>Elatha is on page 163 of Hero.</li> </ul><br /> They are all Titans in cannon.<br /> <br /> Now I am not in anyway involved in the development of any Scion products yet, but I do think the reason the Titans in Titanmomachy are so different is that they are built as potential parents, rather than entities players may have to thwart. I do think they should have Virtues listed and their (Dominion?) associated Purview called out, but Titans can and do have more than one Purview in this edition. Heck Cernunnos the Titan has more Purviews than Cernunnos of the Nemetondevos!<br /> <br /> Demigod Kickstarter Preview 2A mentions Dominion as a kind of communion with a Purview, and much like how I think Callings will scale up by tier, Divine Tier (4) Dominions are something I see heavily connected to Titans at God-level play. Neall calls out the expression of Dominion at Demigod level as 'casual Miracles'. If one can only have a single Dominion Purview, then that is where we get the Purview associated with the Titanic Virtues. So the 'single' Purview listed for Titans, is just the one associated with their Titan Virtues.<br /> <br /> Titanomachy 'updates' a few Titans from the Hero book, but as noted above, it misses others. Additions have been put in here too.<br /> <br /> The Aesir in Hero have a 'Notable Titspawn section, which lists Nidhoggr (the draconic spelling) and Vargr by name. Ymir is listed as a Primordial. Jord and Surtr are not mentioned, so they are introduced in Titanomachy.<br /> The only Titan/Asura listed as such in the Deva section of Hero is Ravanna, who might be the mantle Saita is trying to claim, (as she is clearly still in the Demigod tier). There are hints in both books that an Incarnation may have survived. Ironically Rangda is the only Titan in Titanomachy can see the Orisha/Loa try to take down on their own. Of course I also see them willing to go after Baba Yaga.<br /> Fujin, Raijin and Nezumo are the only Kami Titans listed in the appropriate section of Hero. In my rush to list Titans that aren't pa try t of the Titanomachy, I missed that Nezumo and Namazu are gender alternate mantles of the same myth. My mistake. Still, Goku and Princess Kiyo are Titanomachy only Titans. Although Kiyo and Ao Guang should also have Dragon mantles in my opinion.<br /> All the Manitou Titans are listed in Hero and Titanomachy. Fantastic! Full write ups for everyone!<br /> Same with the Netjer.<br /> The Shen only list Ao Guang and White Eyebrow in Hero, so Kuafu and Su Daji are likewise without known Dominion Purviews and Virtues.<br /> Coyoxauhqui is the only Teotl Titan in Hero and the one used in the listed example of why knowing a Titan's Virtues matter for roleplaying them in chapter 2.<br /> The Theoi write up in Hero lists Cronus, Phoebe (who got erratta'd), Rhea and Typhon in order. So Echidna and Gaea are technically Titanomachy is their first appearances.<br /> The Hero section on the Tuatha Titans lists Balor, Bres, Crom Cruach, (my first choice for an antagonistic Titan not connected to the Titanomachy, but Elatha was another example of a 'good Titan', so I mistakenly went with Nezumo instead) and Domnu. Fun fact, Hero lists Domnu's Purview as Darkness and her Titanomachy write up doesn't have it. Belenus and Cernunnos aren't listed in Hero but are mantles rebuilt from the dead Nemetondevos. So no Virtues for them either and another Pantheon of enemies to boot.<br /> <br /> There are references to additional Titans in the texts (heck Prometheus has 3 scions in the antagonists section of Titanomachy) but that is less 'actionable'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T08:27:02-07:00","id":1413377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geoffrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1413365#post1413365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Elatha is the father of the TDD Titan, Bres (as well as Ogma and the Dagda). By all accounts, he seems like a perfectly reasonable Fomorian: when Bres loses kingship of the TDD and scurries back home, Elatha bluntly tells him he was a bad king. He still tells Bres how to raise an army to take Ireland back, but he's obviously disappointed in his kid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elatha sounds like an awesome Titan.<br /> <br /> For the record, I loved Titanomachy. I think it really expands the Scion universe.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a> good point in the last sentence of your first paragraph.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 09-13-2020, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T08:32:49-07:00","id":1413378,"title":"","content":"I'm going to second the fact that while I quite enjoyed this book, I feel like it didn't really earn a title like &quot;Titanomachy.&quot;<br /> <br /> Are Titans distinct from gods? No? Then it's just a political division? But then why does it exist? Is it just godly beings who are &quot;evil?&quot; that can't be the case, since many of them are outright sympathetic, and haven't done anything to even earn the &quot;Titan&quot; distinction or even provoke conflict at all.<br /> <br /> If anything can be a Titan then nothing is a Titan, and the &quot;Titanomachy&quot; can't possibly exist. I realize that it's mostly a concept that was stretched to too many cultures due to Scion 1e, but I feel like maybe the answer is to just remove the concept of &quot;Titan&quot; entirely except from the perspective of the Theoi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25545-jollycooperative","name":"jollycooperative","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T08:37:25-07:00","id":1413379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jollycooperative</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1413378#post1413378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to second the fact that while I quite enjoyed this book, I feel like it didn't really earn a title like &amp;quot;Titanomachy.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Are Titans distinct from gods? No? Then it's just a political division? But then why does it exist? Is it just godly beings who are &amp;quot;evil?&amp;quot; that can't be the case, since many of them are outright sympathetic, and haven't done anything to even earn the &amp;quot;Titan&amp;quot; distinction or even provoke conflict at all.<br /> <br /> If anything can be a Titan then nothing is a Titan, and the &amp;quot;Titanomachy&amp;quot; can't possibly exist. I realize that it's mostly a concept that was stretched to too many cultures due to Scion 1e, but I feel like maybe the answer is to just remove the concept of &amp;quot;Titan&amp;quot; entirely except from the perspective of the Theoi.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of the major pantheons except the Orisha have some division between gods and Titans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T09:30:28-07:00","id":1413384,"title":"","content":"The point on Titanomachy is that, if they want to respect the myths, the idea of a Titanomachy is bad because most of the pantheons have no such thing as Titans, they may have some adversary gods or an old generation of gods that are not part of the pantheon, or even an adversary pantheon that they may had a long story of adversity, but it\u2019s hard to call any of them are Titans.<br /> <br /> The name Titanomachy is a reference mainly to the idea on 1e, that the gods are fighting a war against one powerful adversary that can face all of them at same time. This adversary never existed, the gods are there because they defeated all their adversaries or are waiting for the final war (or a combination of both).<br /> <br /> The resulting is a book about antagonists centered in the premise that some old gods (called Titans for simplification) are trying to take over the Gods. With that in mind you have the titanspawn (that was the general term for monsters on 1e), that are monsters aligned to the Titans.<br /> <br /> But a great point in the history is that the truth is told by the winners, and the gods are no exception, they are not good, they are not perfect, they are the ones telling the stories, and so, their enemies are the most horrible people in the world.<br /> <br /> The titans are the defeated enemies that may, or may not, be horrible creatures, that may or may not be willing to over throw the gods, that may or may not use their worst weapon to destroy everything as long as they win the war. That is what the gods are telling...<br /> <br /> If you want to make them the real monsters to let the players kill them with no guilty, ok. I personally prefer to make them proper adversaries that you may sympathize before defeating them or even side with them against \u201cthose warmonger gods\u201d. I think those are a much better approach than it was in 1e, while it still gives a nice structure to those that like the good versus evil thing, with a bunch of \u201cevil gods\u201d and monsters to fight.<br /> <br /> If you go to DriveThruRPG and read the reviews of Titanomachy you have the other side of the complaining, that the Titans are forced to exist just to fill the gap left from 1e, that it goes against the myths, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T12:20:33-07:00","id":1413416,"title":"","content":"If being a Titan is a political thing and the &quot;war&quot; is conducted from two sides of the same coin -- I think the way the Sabbat and the Pure are presented are great examples of how antagonists can be written with a lot of nuance (and playability) but still clearly be the &quot;bad guys.&quot;<br /> <br /> The way the Pure evolved in WtF is a great example of this. Even though it took many, many books to finally get one dedicated to the Pure (and really make them playable), it was clear from the core what their motivations were, how they organized, how they self-identified, and, ultimately, the nature of their role as antagonists.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, you can have nuance and sophisticated enemies even if they basically look a lot like the protagonists. The key is spending the wordcount to present the case to the reader and making sure the authors all have the same vision for whats going on.<br /> <br /> Part of the problem I see here is that players are having to read between the lines and come to their own conclusions. People are already looking at rewrites. That really shouldnt be, especially in a book that is supposed to define the Titans and their threat. Some clear language right at the top seems appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaponized Ink: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/288291/Werewolf-The-Savage-Age-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: The Savage Age!</a> </span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":11548,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","user":"Coyoteintx","date":". 09-13-2020, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","name":"Coyoteintx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11548_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T13:17:14-07:00","id":1413429,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a> Titanomachy is less central in 2E for the very reasons you're stating, but as a concept applicable in the World, the idea that pantheons interacting and having alliances with each other (generally not a mythic concept save for the Aesir and Vanir) would apply shared nomenclature to their &quot;enemies who threaten the order the pantheons uphold&quot; is not unreasonable. Obviously the fact that they still interact with those enemies quite differently from each other is a major highlighted element of the setting - from hardline war and imprisonment parties (Theoi, Deva, Teteo, kinda the Netjeru), too &quot;keep actively in check, but assimilate as much as possible as well&quot; (Tuatha, Aesir, Shen), to deal solely in a case by case basis as needed, recognizing &quot;Titans&quot; but not necessarily a common &quot;Titanomachy (Kami, Manitou), to &quot;what the fuck are you talking about&quot; (Orisha).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-13-2020, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T14:35:07-07:00","id":1413443,"title":"","content":"Here is part of the ad copy on the DriveThru landing page...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i><b>The second war against the Gods fast approaches.<br /> <br /> Are you prepared?</b></i></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><b>Scion: Titanomachy</b> has everything a Storyguide needs to bring the Second Titanomachy \u2014 a phase in the eternal cold war against the Gods \u2014 to their <b>Scion Second Edition </b>games.</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> From that, it doesnt appear that 'Titanomachy&quot; is being downplayed or a thing specific to one or two pantheons. There is a lot implied by those handful of phrases - and &quot;Titanomachy&quot; is presented as a major setting/plot point. The god-titan cold war is a thing. There is a a coming war against the Titans. In fact is has a proper name, &quot;The Second Titanomachy.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, where is that in this book? If many (if not most) of the Titans are set up as sympathetic and generally not very different than the Gods... then where is the motivation and imperative for the 'Second Titanomachy' coming from?<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think there is a pretty significant disconnect about how the ad copy sells the game and what is contained therein.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaponized Ink: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/288291/Werewolf-The-Savage-Age-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: The Savage Age!</a> </span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":11548,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","user":"Coyoteintx","date":". 09-13-2020, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","name":"Coyoteintx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11548_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T15:15:06-07:00","id":1413448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coyoteintx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1413443#post1413443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is part of the ad copy on the DriveThru landing page...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i><b>The second war against the Gods fast approaches.<br /> <br /> Are you prepared?</b></i></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><b>Scion: Titanomachy</b> has everything a Storyguide needs to bring the Second Titanomachy \u2014 a phase in the eternal cold war against the Gods \u2014 to their <b>Scion Second Edition </b>games.</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> From that, it doesnt appear that 'Titanomachy&quot; is being downplayed or a thing specific to one or two pantheons. There is a lot implied by those handful of phrases - and &quot;Titanomachy&quot; is presented as a major setting/plot point. The god-titan cold war is a thing. There is a a coming war against the Titans. In fact is has a proper name, &quot;The Second Titanomachy.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, where is that in this book? If many (if not most) of the Titans are set up as sympathetic and generally not very different than the Gods... then where is the motivation and imperative for the 'Second Titanomachy' coming from?<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think there is a pretty significant disconnect about how the ad copy sells the game and what is contained therein.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's not being downplayed IN THIS SUPPLEMENT. This is a supplement focused on Titanomachy stories. But the fact that it can have a dedicated supplement as opposed to being central in Hero-Demigod-God is it being decentered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T18:53:02-07:00","id":1413473,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> how much do you think the Titanomachy will affect future Scion products?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T19:30:43-07:00","id":1413478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1413473#post1413473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> how much do you think the Titanomachy will affect future Scion products?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's generally bad game design for future books to require possession of a specific supplement, besides stuff like &quot;see Titanomachy for more on the Titan Callings&quot; as a side note. We can already see in the Demigod draft that conflict with Titans does not appear more narratively central than it was in Hero. Titanomachy is not getting sidelined as extra-canonical, but it's also not the new heart of the game. We already know that God is going to be more concerned with making a Creation Myth to form a new Pantheon, or Incarnation play, than on &quot;battling worldforms laying siege to the Godrealms&quot; ala 1e. That element may be there too! But it won't be the expected default of God play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T20:45:54-07:00","id":1413484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1413478#post1413478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's generally bad game design for future books to require possession of a specific supplement, besides stuff like &amp;quot;see Titanomachy for more on the Titan Callings&amp;quot; as a side note. We can already see in the Demigod draft that conflict with Titans does not appear more narratively central than it was in Hero. Titanomachy is not getting sidelined as extra-canonical, but it's also not the new heart of the game. We already know that God is going to be more concerned with making a Creation Myth to form a new Pantheon, or Incarnation play, than on &amp;quot;battling worldforms laying siege to the Godrealms&amp;quot; ala 1e. That element may be there too! But it won't be the expected default of God play.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds great \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T21:38:32-07:00","id":1413492,"title":"","content":"So all in all if your looking for a &quot;book of things to fight&quot; this is ultimately a poor choice correct? As ultimately thats something thats kind of missing from Scion right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25723-kite474","name":"Kite474","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T22:39:42-07:00","id":1413496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kite474</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1413492#post1413492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So all in all if your looking for a &quot;book of things to fight&quot; this is ultimately a poor choice correct? As ultimately thats something thats kind of missing from Scion right now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The monsters and Titan Scion foes in the antagonist chapter should be useful toward that end, but it's not the dedicated focus of the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T23:02:17-07:00","id":1413497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kite474</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1413492#post1413492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So all in all if your looking for a &quot;book of things to fight&quot; this is ultimately a poor choice correct? As ultimately thats something thats kind of missing from Scion right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the book has a huge number of \u201cthings to fight\u201d, explanations on how to make them even more powerful (or less powerful, if you want).<br /> <br /> But, if you are looking for reasons to fight those things, it\u2019s not the book. It has monsters you may want to fight, actually most of them are pretty straight forward enemies, but you have also monsters that you may want to side with, even they being \u201cthe enemy\u201d, and monster that just don\u2019t care if they are the enemies, they don\u2019t even care about \u201cthis war thing going on for eons\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T09:04:58-07:00","id":1413571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1413497#post1413497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, the book has a huge number of \u201cthings to fight\u201d, explanations on how to make them even more powerful (or less powerful, if you want).<br /> <br /> But, if you are looking for reasons to fight those things, it\u2019s not the book. It has monsters you may want to fight, actually most of them are pretty straight forward enemies, but you have also monsters that you may want to side with, even they being \u201cthe enemy\u201d, and monster that just don\u2019t care if they are the enemies, they don\u2019t even care about \u201cthis war thing going on for eons\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. People who think that this book is somehow against the grain of 2E need to pick up Mythical Denizens - the freaking Wendigo has some sympathetic traits. Frankly, Scion 2E is openly against the idea that &quot;Titanspawn&quot; means &quot;Evil.&quot; It means &quot;enemy/rival of the traditional divine order.&quot; And then openly pointing out how little of a commonality that is.<br /> <br /> Frankly, if that were the case, the Orishas' subsection wouldn't be &quot;yeah, Titans aren't really a thing.&quot; And in Demigod, the Atua's perspective would not be &quot;...why do you think there's a a difference?&quot;<br /> <br /> Titan, in 2E, is a deliberately messy definition, because it's a title imposed on them by outside forces. And those outside forces have completely different definitions of what a Titan is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T16:46:27-07:00","id":1413649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1413571#post1413571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-snip-<br /> Titan, in 2E, is a deliberately messy definition, because it's a title <b>imposed on them by outside forces. And those outside forces have completely different definitions of what a Titan is.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine, because I really wish someone had articulated this earlier. This is what I mean when I say it is mostly political.<br /> Heck, some of the 'good' Titans are likely labelled as such because they make the gods <b>uncomfortable</b>; Rhea and Elatha are good examples of that sort thing in theory. Titan Callings, Virtues and Dominion Purviews are just the sort of thing prompts that kind of reaction from certain powerful deities, as a VERY general trend.<br /> Gods still think of themselves as people, as opposed to personifications of reality, wrapped in narrative. Apparently it is rude to remind them.<br /> <br /> I'd like to stress that it only certain pantheons (primarily in the Hero book) that appear to be pushing for the idea of the Titanomachy. Heck the Tuatha de Danann, the pantheon with the most organized Titans, outright acknowledge the divide is political and intermarry. The Aesir aren't far behind. The Theoi are one of the pantheons pushing for it and they have the most 'good' Titans!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T07:23:00-07:00","id":1413769,"title":"","content":"Hmm not sure how to feel about that. At the end of the day Scion is a game that still has combat as a key part of it and to take the biggest antagonist and just not make them antagonist at all feels less like grey morality or being clever and just makes it all annoyingly awkward. If the game had less combat as part of it or was more focused from the beginning of the gods being the &quot;real&quot; bad guys that would be fine but it doesn't do much of either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25723-kite474","name":"Kite474","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T07:28:58-07:00","id":1413771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kite474</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1413769#post1413769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm not sure how to feel about that. At the end of the day Scion is a game that still has combat as a key part of it and to take the biggest antagonist and just not make them antagonist at all feels less like grey morality or being clever and just makes it all annoyingly awkward. If the game had less combat as part of it or was more focused from the beginning of the gods being the &quot;real&quot; bad guys that would be fine but it doesn't do much of either.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are plenty of beings who are unambiguously evil to fight. But no one's splat name make them that. Characters have to actually employ moral judgment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T07:30:14-07:00","id":1413772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1413571#post1413571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah. People who think that this book is somehow against the grain of 2E need to pick up Mythical Denizens - the freaking Wendigo has some sympathetic traits. Frankly, Scion 2E is openly against the idea that &amp;quot;Titanspawn&amp;quot; means &amp;quot;Evil.&amp;quot; It means &amp;quot;enemy/rival of the traditional divine order.&amp;quot; And then openly pointing out how little of a commonality that is.<br /> <br /> Frankly, if that were the case, the Orishas' subsection wouldn't be &amp;quot;yeah, Titans aren't really a thing.&amp;quot; And in Demigod, the Atua's perspective would not be &amp;quot;...why do you think there's a a difference?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Titan, in 2E, is a deliberately messy definition, because it's a title imposed on them by outside forces. And those outside forces have completely different definitions of what a Titan is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this facet of 2e. Also, the Orisha, Loa and Atua all make no distinction between gods and Titans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T07:55:36-07:00","id":1413776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1413571#post1413571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah. People who think that this book is somehow against the grain of 2E need to pick up Mythical Denizens - the freaking Wendigo has some sympathetic traits. Frankly, Scion 2E is openly against the idea that &quot;Titanspawn&quot; means &quot;Evil.&quot; It means &quot;enemy/rival of the traditional divine order.&quot; And then openly pointing out how little of a commonality that is.<br /> <br /> Frankly, if that were the case, the Orishas' subsection wouldn't be &quot;yeah, Titans aren't really a thing.&quot; And in Demigod, the Atua's perspective would not be &quot;...why do you think there's a a difference?&quot;<br /> <br /> Titan, in 2E, is a deliberately messy definition, because it's a title imposed on them by outside forces. And those outside forces have completely different definitions of what a Titan is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the complaints of being against the grain of 2E was the degree of liberties taken with some of the myths - not just filling in gaps, but rewrites with major ramifications. My biggest beef is presenting Odin and his brothers violating Hospitality, which from Norse ethics is a greater crime than any of the actual horrible crimes attributed to Odin by the Eddas, so it would serve to recontextualize the ENTIRETY of Norse Mythology.<br /> <br /> In cases in myth where an Aesir kills a jotunn host, they are very careful to make sure the host violates hospitality first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T08:17:09-07:00","id":1413781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1413649#post1413649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Emphasis mine, because I really wish someone had articulated this earlier. This is what I mean when I say it is mostly political.<br /> Heck, some of the 'good' Titans are likely labelled as such because they make the gods <b>uncomfortable</b>; Rhea and Elatha are good examples of that sort thing in theory. Titan Callings, Virtues and Dominion Purviews are just the sort of thing prompts that kind of reaction from certain powerful deities, as a VERY general trend.<br /> Gods still think of themselves as people, as opposed to personifications of reality, wrapped in narrative. Apparently it is rude to remind them.<br /> <br /> I'd like to stress that it only certain pantheons (primarily in the Hero book) that appear to be pushing for the idea of the Titanomachy. Heck the Tuatha de Danann, the pantheon with the most organized Titans, outright acknowledge the divide is political and intermarry. The Aesir aren't far behind. The Theoi are one of the pantheons pushing for it and they have the most 'good' Titans!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is the sort of stuff that the book really needs. Some real deep dives into how the various pantheons use the term &quot;Titan&quot; (or the equivilent). I see Titanomachy as a golden opportunity to talk about what it means to be a Titan and how the pantheons use Titan-ostracism to advance their own ends. <br /> <br /> There are some cool insights on this forum, but understanding here doesnt equate to understanding by readers who dont frequent this forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaponized Ink: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/288291/Werewolf-The-Savage-Age-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: The Savage Age!</a> </span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","name":"Coyoteintx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11548_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-10T14:30:10-07:00","id":1417571,"title":"","content":"So uh, has anyone else noticed that the sample Creature don\u2019t make sense according to the rules set put in Hero? Like for example the Fenrir Pups, have three qualities yet still have the standard 9 dice that three dot Creatures get","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-10T21:46:13-07:00","id":1417596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1417571#post1417571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So uh, has anyone else noticed that the sample Creature don\u2019t make sense according to the rules set put in Hero? Like for example the Fenrir Pups, have three qualities yet still have the standard 9 dice that three dot Creatures get</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I saw that, I just scale them back to the appropriate levels for the game I'm ST'ing. I think they were designed to be antagonists first, and actual usable Birthrights second, which could explain the discrepancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T11:43:00-07:00","id":1417672,"title":"","content":"You should read the old Mage books. They constantly had NPCs whose stats didn't begin to match their described powers and characteristics. They clearly choose to maintain tradition around here ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T11:55:02-07:00","id":1417674,"title":"","content":"The Creature rules just aren't very good. They don't really work for the antagonists presented in Hero, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T12:59:37-07:00","id":1417686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1417674#post1417674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Creature rules just aren't very good. They don't really work for the antagonists presented in Hero, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>While nowhere near as confusing as the rules for Guides I agree that I am having trouble putting Creatures together for my players and had to seek help here for it. It's sad that they are not as simple and well put together as the rules for Relics and Followers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T13:15:41-07:00","id":1417690,"title":"","content":"What\u2019s confusing about Guides? The only problems I\u2019ve had with them is trying to think of good Guide Stunts, but for Creatures I can\u2019t wait till we get the expansion in the Demigod Companion, cause they so desperately need one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T14:09:53-07:00","id":1417699,"title":"","content":"My advice for creatures (as a storyguide that had a player who just had to spend all her exp on more creatures).<br /> Until the creature expansion that was a stretch goal for demigod comes out just use the follower rules to create the creature. With Flairs &quot;costing 1 dot per flairs you add. <br /> Much less of a headache that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T18:58:05-07:00","id":1417747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1417571#post1417571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So uh, has anyone else noticed that the sample Creature don\u2019t make sense according to the rules set put in Hero? Like for example the Fenrir Pups, have three qualities yet still have the standard 9 dice that three dot Creatures get</div> </div> </div> </div>It has been reported for the errata, right?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T20:15:40-07:00","id":1417758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1417686#post1417686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While nowhere near as confusing as the rules for Guides I agree that I am having trouble putting Creatures together for my players and had to seek help here for it. It's sad that they are not as simple and well put together as the rules for Relics and Followers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll echo &quot;What's wrong with Guide?&quot;<br /> <br /> Guides are great. My only stumbling point are the Guide Stunts, and 80% of those can be solved by stealing an existing Guide Stunt from a pre-written Guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T20:27:03-07:00","id":1417760,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll admit they did trip me up for a while with stunts, and also I can see them being a bit odd with how they are somewhat less customizable then the rest of the corebook Birthrights like how the Covenant is less custom then Cults in the Companion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T03:54:23-07:00","id":1417787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1417758#post1417758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll echo &quot;What's wrong with Guide?&quot;<br /> <br /> Guides are great. My only stumbling point are the Guide Stunts, and 80% of those can be solved by stealing an existing Guide Stunt from a pre-written Guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will agree that Guide is probably a fun thing if you understand it. My problem is precisely that, trying to understand the stunt rules and Asset Skills that belong to Guides, both in the more or less non-existent rules about how to design your own Guides as well as not quite understanding the mechanics of existing Guide's stunts.<br /> <br /> English is not my first language but I doubt that is the cause of the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T03:57:36-07:00","id":1417788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1417699#post1417699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My advice for creatures (as a storyguide that had a player who just had to spend all her exp on more creatures).<br /> Until the creature expansion that was a stretch goal for demigod comes out just use the follower rules to create the creature. With Flairs &quot;costing 1 dot per flairs you add.<br /> Much less of a headache that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot escape thinking that is an unsatisfying solution. Followers are more or less like equipment in the rules: you use them with your own Leadership skill as if they were an extension of you with limited range of capabilities on their own. Applying that to a mythological creature that is supposed to be a sidekick seems a bit unsatisfying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T07:17:41-07:00","id":1417810,"title":"","content":"I mean Followers are also meant to represent sidekicks, like the Enkidu to your Gilgamesh. And honestly most Creatures tend to be more like living equipment narratively speaking anyways, they don\u2019t usually do much on their own in mythology","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T13:40:19-07:00","id":1417899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1417787#post1417787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will agree that Guide is probably a fun thing if you understand it. My problem is precisely that, trying to understand the stunt rules and Asset Skills that belong to Guides, both in the more or less non-existent rules about how to design your own Guides as well as not quite understanding the mechanics of existing Guide's stunts.<br /> <br /> English is not my first language but I doubt that is the cause of the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so, here's how I break it down:<br /> <br /> - Guide Stunts are tricks that your Guides taught you, and the Asset Skills are the things that they teach you. The effects of Guide Stunts can overlap (thus my stealing a lot of them) but they apply in areas where you tap the Guide for extra dice in the Asset Skills. So the context of the Stunts come from the Asset Skills.<br /> <br /> Example: Let's say you have a Guide Stunt that lets you improve someone's attitude towards you as a special Stunt. That Stunt can actually be applied to different Guides, but the Stunt will only be used in the Asset Skill. So if you have, say, Scathach as a Guide, and her Asset Skills are Close Combat and Athletics, then you can apply her Guide Stunt in situatiosn using either Close Combat or Athletics. Combine the two, and you get something like this:<br /> <br /> &quot;Wow, you made that attack in such an impressive way that I can't help but admire you now&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Thanks, Scathach taught me that any attack worth making is worth doing impressively&quot;<br /> <br /> If you think about it this way, then you can open some variety. Take a Stunt that allows you to remove a field condition and tie it to, say, Survival or Culture, and usually use it to clear things like overgrown forests. Boom, you just did the legwork for making a Dryad Guide and can add on the Fun stuff like a Purview or a unique Knack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T14:11:27-07:00","id":1417909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1417899#post1417899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, so, here's how I break it down:<br /> <br /> - Guide Stunts are tricks that your Guides taught you, and the Asset Skills are the things that they teach you. The effects of Guide Stunts can overlap (thus my stealing a lot of them) but they apply in areas where you tap the Guide for extra dice in the Asset Skills. So the context of the Stunts come from the Asset Skills.<br /> <br /> Example: Let's say you have a Guide Stunt that lets you improve someone's attitude towards you as a special Stunt. That Stunt can actually be applied to different Guides, but the Stunt will only be used in the Asset Skill. So if you have, say, Scathach as a Guide, and her Asset Skills are Close Combat and Athletics, then you can apply her Guide Stunt in situatiosn using either Close Combat or Athletics. Combine the two, and you get something like this:<br /> <br /> &quot;Wow, you made that attack in such an impressive way that I can't help but admire you now&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Thanks, Scathach taught me that any attack worth making is worth doing impressively&quot;<br /> <br /> If you think about it this way, then you can open some variety. Take a Stunt that allows you to remove a field condition and tie it to, say, Survival or Culture, and usually use it to clear things like overgrown forests. Boom, you just did the legwork for making a Dryad Guide and can add on the Fun stuff like a Purview or a unique Knack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow thanks, I think it is all a lot clearer now! I will have to explain this in a good way to my players then, see if they get interested in taking Guides in the future.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T14:29:49-07:00","id":1417917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1417899#post1417899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if you have, say, Scathach as a Guide, and her Asset Skills are Close Combat and Athletics, then you can apply her Guide Stunt in situatiosn using either Close Combat or Athletics. Combine the two, and you get something like this:<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Wow, you made that attack in such an impressive way that I can't help but admire you now&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Thanks, Scathach taught me that any attack worth making is worth doing impressively&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sun Wukong would be proud... I mean Son Goku... making friend by beating them pretty hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T16:33:10-07:00","id":1417947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411304-scion-titanomachy-pdf?p=1417909#post1417909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow thanks, I think it is all a lot clearer now! I will have to explain this in a good way to my players then, see if they get interested in taking Guides in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad I was able to help!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}